# Org repository discovery (API SSOT)

For org-wide automation, **which repositories exist** is defined by the GitHub
org API — not by whichever directories happen to be checked out under a scan root.

## Do

- Discover membership with `rp_discover_org_repos` / `rp_discover_audit_repos`,
  or the same `gh api "orgs/${org}/repos" --paginate` pattern (see
  `scripts/github-repo-lint` enforcer and `scripts/dep-updater`
  `discover_batch_all_org_repo_names`).
- Treat scan-root / local clones as a **workspace**: resolve a slug to a checkout
  when work needs the filesystem (`rp_resolve_local_repo_dir`, dep-updater
  `--scan-root` index). If no clone exists, **report the gap** — do not pretend
  the repo is outside the org.
- Default org is `the-hcma` (`rp_DEFAULT_ORG` / `DEP_UPDATER_ORG` /
  `GITHUB_REPO_LINT_ORG` as appropriate). Prefer env/flag overrides over
  hardcoding sibling repo names (see `no-hardcoded-org-repos.mdc`).

## Do not

- Drive “all org repos” jobs solely from `find` / directory listing under a scan
  root (that silently drops repos that were never cloned, e.g. a new org project).
- Skip missing-clone visibility in email/logs for batch/enforcer-style reports.

## Reference implementations

| Tool | Membership | Local clone |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `github-repo-lint --enforcer` | `rp_discover_org_repos` | not required for audit |
| `secret-audit --all` | `rp_discover_org_repos` | optional (markers) |
| `dep-updater --batch --all` | org API, then map to `--scan-root` clones | required to mutate |

When adding a new org-wide script or timer, start from the API list, then attach
local paths — never the reverse.

